# Bot versions and benches

- `btk.bot.vNN` packages are frozen reference opponents. Do not edit them, even to fix bugs.
- New behaviour goes into `btk.bot.current`. Anything tunable is a public field of `btk.bot.Params`
  (default = what ships); expose feature switches as boolean params so ablations run as
  `gradlew bench -Pbot1="current?FLAG=0" -Pbot2=current`.
- A change is finished only after `gradlew bench -Pbot1=current -Pbot2=v<prev> -Pgames=300 -Pmaps=replays/cg`
  and a row in `docs/BOTS.md` (win rate with CI, avg score diff). Promote to a new frozen version
  when A >= 55% and the CI excludes 50%: copy `bot/current` to `bot/vNN`, rename the class with a
  `VNN` suffix, change `name()` to `"vNN"`, register it in `BotFactory`.
- Record failed experiments in `docs/DEVLOG.md` too (hypothesis, numbers, why rejected).
- Before saying a bot is "ready to submit": `gradlew submit` and `gradlew procCheck` must pass with
  zero timeouts.
